    feat(task-03): add SRS, architecture, data model and a verified local setup[m
    [m
    Design the system and prove the development setup actually works.[m
    [m
    Requirements and design[m
    - SRS summary: 20 functional requirements (FR-01..FR-20) and 11 non-functional[m
      requirements (NFR-01..NFR-11), each traced to the user story that specifies it[m
      and the acceptance criteria that prove it.[m
    - Four diagrams authored as Mermaid and rendered to PNG+SVG: use-case view,[m
      layered architecture, ER model and the approval state machine.[m
    - Data model: 5 tables with constraints, including unique(student, course,[m
      session_date) which is what enforces "no duplicate records for a session", and[m
      the attendance-percentage rule that counts APPROVED records only.[m
    - Endpoint list, externalised configuration table and a fixed port map (8080 app,[m
      8081 container, 8082 Tomcat, 8090 Jenkins, 5000 registry) to pre-empt the port[m
      collisions flagged as risk R5.[m
    [m
    Application skeleton[m
    - Maven project: Spring Boot 3.3.13, Java 17, war packaging with the embedded[m
      Tomcat scoped provided, so one artefact both runs locally and deploys to a[m
      standalone Tomcat 10.1.[m
    - Baseline security filter chain, landing page proving the Thymeleaf path, and[m
      externalised settings (port, datasource, attendance threshold) read from[m
      environment variables with local defaults.[m
    - Four smoke tests: context loads, health endpoint is public and UP, landing page[m
      renders the configured threshold, and a protected URL is intercepted.[m
    [m
    One real defect, found by running rather than by testing[m
    - The build passed while the application could not start: the smoke tests override[m
      the datasource URL with in-memory H2, so the file-mode default was never[m
      exercised. H2 2.x refuses AUTO_SERVER=TRUE combined with DB_CLOSE_ON_EXIT=FALSE;[m
      both were removed. Recorded in docs/03-architecture.md section 9.2 because it is[m
      exactly the gap the Selenium gate, container health check and Ansible[m
      verification exist to close.[m
    - A test assertion was also corrected: it expected a 302 from a protected URL, but[m
      TestRestTemplate follows redirects, so it now asserts the login form is served[m
      in place of the protected resource.[m
    [m
    Tooling[m
    - scripts/app-control.sh starts, stops and waits on the app using an explicit PID[m
      file, because a `pkill -f spring-boot:run` pattern also matches the shell that[m
      invokes it and kills the caller.[m
    [m
    Verified: mvn -B clean package BUILD SUCCESS with 4/4 tests, application UP in 8s,[m
